{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WDyjQiDRWdWzSShMpdNniG","type":"tool_result","content":"219:## Git and commits\n220-\n221-One branch per story or per fix cycle. Commit message: `<type>: <description>`, one line, in English,\n222-whatever the language of the session or of the file changed; the types are `feat`, `fix`,\n223-`refactor`, `docs`, `test`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`. The message states the resulting behaviour, never\n224-the process that produced it: no work-package reference, no review round, no attribution, no\n225-`Co-Authored-By`. Nothing is pushed by an automaton; `gh` for every GitHub operation, never the API\n226-directly; no issue is created by an automaton.\n227-\n228-## What is written by hand, and what is observed\n229-\n230-By hand: a product decision in `specs/adr/`, the order of the work in `specs/plan.yaml`, where\n231-the owner marks `prete: oui` the epics that run without them, and, for every epic added to the plan,\n232-its dossier in `specs/epics/`, which the plan entry cites as `source:` and the session that writes\n233-its stories reads. The story and the registry entry are\n234-written by hand when the owner drives the story; in a run without them, a session writes them under\n235-the rules of this file. Everything else is observed and recorded by the tool at the moment it\n236-observes it: a red and its message, a Preflight and its revision, a review round and its findings,\n237-the acceptance run and the owner's agreement, the landing. Evidence is written once, in the record of\n238-the step that produced it; elsewhere it is cited. A copy drifts from the code it describes.\n239-\n240-## The cycle without the owner\n241-\n242-`npm run cycle -- suite` runs, one after the other, the epics that `specs/plan.yaml` marks\n243-`prete: oui`, in the order of the plan. For each: the next story of the plan is written by a session\n244-when none is listed to do, it is driven to landing as above, the plan marks it landed, and the epic\n/** Scope entries are directory prefixes (`src/`), exact files, or simple `*` globs on one segment. */\nexport function matchesScope(path: string, pattern: string): boolean {\n\tif (pattern === \"\" || pattern === \".\" || pattern === \"**\") return true;\n\tif (pattern.endsWith(\"/\")) return path === pattern.slice(0, -1) || path.startsWith(pattern);\n\tif (pattern.includes(\"*\")) {\n\t\tconst re = new RegExp(\n\t\t\t`^${pattern\n\t\t\t\t.split(\"**\")\n\t\t\t\t.map((p) => p.split(\"*\").map(escapeRe).join(\"[^/]*\"))\n\t\t\t\t.join(\".*\")}$`,\n\t\t);\n\t\treturn re.test(path);\n\t}\n\treturn path === pattern || path.startsWith(`${pattern}/`);\n}\n\n/**\n * Whether `path` names what the protected `pattern` names on a volume that ignores case and Unicode form, as macOS\n * does by default: a tool that opens `stryker.conf.json` there reads `Stryker.conf.json` or `ſtryker.conf.json`.\n * Folding both sides refuses more on a volume that tells them apart, never less.\n */\nfunction matchesProtected(path: string, pattern: string): boolean {\n\treturn matchesScope(foldName(path), foldName(pattern));\n}\n\nfunction foldName(s: string): string {\n\treturn s.normalize(\"NFKD\").toUpperCase().toLowerCase();\n}\n\nfunction escapeRe(s: string): string {\n\treturn s.replace(/[.+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, \"\\\\$&\");\n}\n\nexport interface ProtectedPaths {\n\t/** Every path this candidate changed, whatever it is. */\n\tchanged: string[];\n\t/** The changed paths but a prepared or complement file the candidate holds as the kernel wrote it. */\n\tproduced: string[];\n\t/** Changes to a protected path the frozen protocol allows. */\n\tallowed: string[];\n\t/** Changes to a protected path nothing allows: the producer altered an oracle. */\n\taltered: string[];\n}\n\n/**\n * Each path a candidate changed under a submodule of the reference, or the boundary itself, with that\n * submodule: its files belong to another repository, and a commit of the project canno